From 44e103b037c813f0499312483208febccc2b7f02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:39:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): separate recovery evidence from model
 obligations [daveey]

Problem: the model-neutral create gate rejected legacy titles and diagnostic/provenance text, stranding recovery and spend-stop producers. Why: co-occurring words were treated as route obligations, and kernel siblings copied historical fields into active prose. Detection gap: earlier real-producer tests covered only continuation/no-progress and placement forwarding.

Bind obligations to route grammar; retain source title/error/history losslessly as inert evidence while keeping active recovery/safety instructions. Cover remaining title-quoting kernel producer families and capability courier siblings; preserve active action refusal, independent execution custody, dependencies, spend/containment and quota/probe gates.

Proof: unchanged independent probes 5pass9fail; focused78pass; additional prior-head audit9pass11fail versus current20pass; importing/facade116files2760pass0fail1skip retriesOFF; full scripts/check21GREEN. Full fleet remediation/deployment acceptance remains open on t_b76fc0ced1eeacb2.
